[00:00.000 --> 00:02.500]  Quick hair creation and animation in Blender.
[00:02.500 --> 00:08.000]  Take a UV sphere, right-click, shade smooth, go to material properties, add two materials.
[00:08.000 --> 00:11.000]  One for the sphere, one for the hair.
[00:11.000 --> 00:15.000]  Set the hair material to Principled Hair BSDF.
[00:15.000 --> 00:17.000]  Go to weight paint mode.
[00:17.000 --> 00:19.000]  Paint the area you want hair to grow.
[00:19.000 --> 00:21.000]  Rename the vertex group if you want.
[00:21.000 --> 00:22.000]  Add a particle system.
[00:22.000 --> 00:24.000]  Switch from Emitter to Hair.
[00:24.000 --> 00:28.000]  Select the hair material and set Vertex Groups to Hair Group.
[00:28.000 --> 00:29.000]  Adjust hair length.
[00:29.000 --> 00:31.000]  Comb particles in Edit Mode.
[00:31.000 --> 00:34.000]  Then return to Object Mode when satisfied.
[00:34.000 --> 00:37.000]  In Particle System, enable Children.
[00:37.000 --> 00:40.000]  Set to Interpolated and set values to 200.
[00:40.000 --> 00:47.000]  In Render Properties, set the render engine to Cycles and turn on Hair Dynamics for automatic animation.
[00:47.000 --> 00:49.000]  Set pin goal strength to 0.460.
[00:49.000 --> 00:52.000]  Subscribe for more Blender tips on Filmtouche.
